kiln::semantic

  × systemd-boot cannot boot an OSTree system
   ╭─[system.toml:6:11]
 5 │ [boot]
 6 │ loader  = "systemd-boot"
   ·           ───────┬──────
   ·                  ╰── not available
 7 │ timeout = 3
   ╰────
  help: OSTree keeps /boot/loader as a symlink pair so that entry swaps are atomic, and
        UEFI firmware reads only FAT — so /boot cannot be the ESP, and systemd-boot
        cannot read the ext4 /boot OSTree needs. Kiln uses GRUB2 through libostree's own
        backend instead; remove this line to get it.
